{
  "$schema": "https://json.schemastore.org/sarif-2.1.0.json",
  "runs": [
    {
      "results": [
        {
          "level": "note",
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "server.js%3A78-102%2C%20app/routes/session.js%3A116%2C%20app/routes/error.js%3A10-12"
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "Session cookie lacks `httpOnly`/`secure`; no regeneration on login; error page echoes raw error\n\nThe session is served over plain HTTP with default cookie options (no `httpOnly`, no `secure`, default `connect.sid` name) and `saveUninitialized: true`. Login sets `req.session.userId` without `regenerate()`, so a pre-login session ID fixed by an attacker becomes authenticated. The global error handler renders the error object directly into an unescaped template, exposing internal messages (for example Mongo `$where` evaluation errors containing the injected payload). The login failure path also logs the raw `userName`, allowing CRLF log forging. These amplify F6 (cookie theft via XSS) rather than being independently exploitable."
          },
          "ruleId": "sast/CWE-1004/low",
          "ruleIndex": 0
        },
        {
          "level": "warning",
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "app/routes/profile.js%3A59-61"
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "ReDoS via nested quantifier on bank routing validator\n\nThe pattern `/([0-9]+)+\\#/` has a nested unbounded quantifier. A `bankRouting` value of thirty or more digits followed by a non-`#` character causes exponential backtracking in V8's regex engine and blocks the single Node event loop, denying service to all users."
          },
          "ruleId": "sast/CWE-1333/medium",
          "ruleIndex": 1
        },
        {
          "level": "warning",
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "server.js%3A104-113%2C%20app/views/profile.html%3A73"
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "CSRF protection disabled on all state-changing POST handlers\n\nThe `csurf` middleware is commented out, so `res.locals.csrftoken` is never set and every form's hidden `_csrf` field renders empty. POST `/profile`, `/contributions`, `/benefits`, and `/memos` accept cross-origin form submissions from a logged-in victim's browser, letting an attacker change their bank account number or (via F1) execute code as the victim's session."
          },
          "ruleId": "sast/CWE-352/medium",
          "ruleIndex": 2
        },
        {
          "level": "warning",
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "config/env/all.js%3A8-9%2C%20artifacts/db-reset.js%3A15-18"
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "Hardcoded session secret, crypto key, and seeded admin credentials\n\nThe express-session signing secret and the AES key are literal strings in a public repository, and `production.js` overrides nothing. The seed script creates `admin / Admin_123`, `user1 / User1_123`, `user2 / User2_123`. Anyone who knows the project can log in as admin on a seeded deployment with no prior access. A private TLS key is also committed under `artifacts/cert/`."
          },
          "ruleId": "sast/CWE-798/medium",
          "ruleIndex": 3
        },
        {
          "level": "warning",
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "app/routes/index.js%3A70-73"
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "Open redirect on `/learn?url=`\n\nThe handler redirects to whatever the `url` query parameter contains. A phishing link such as `/learn?url=https://evil.example/login` carries the trusted origin and lands a logged-in victim on an attacker page."
          },
          "ruleId": "sast/CWE-601/medium",
          "ruleIndex": 4
        },
        {
          "level": "warning",
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "app/data/user-dao.js%3A25%2C%20%3A61"
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "Passwords stored and compared in plaintext\n\n`addUser` persists the raw password, and `validateLogin` compares with `===`. `bcrypt-nodejs` is imported but unused. Combined with F3 (dump via `$where`) or F5 (full user docs to template), the plaintext passwords are directly retrievable by any authenticated user; this is the stated precondition for the AC:H rating."
          },
          "ruleId": "sast/CWE-256/medium",
          "ruleIndex": 5
        },
        {
          "level": "error",
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "server.js%3A135-137%2C%20app/views/layout.html%3A75"
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "Global template autoescape disabled; stored and reflected XSS\n\nSwig autoescaping is turned off globally, so every `{{ }}` in every template emits raw HTML. Stored XSS: a user sets `firstName` to `<script>...</script>` via `/profile`; it is rendered unescaped in their own navbar, in every other user's view via `/allocations/{{id}}` (F4), and in the admin's `/benefits` table. Reflected XSS: on login failure, `userName` is echoed into the login form value attribute; on profile validation failure, raw `firstName` is placed into an `href` (`javascript:` URI). The `encodeForHTML` on `website` is the only encoding and is the wrong context for the `href` where `firstNameSafeString` is used."
          },
          "ruleId": "sast/CWE-79/high",
          "ruleIndex": 6
        },
        {
          "level": "error",
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "app/routes/index.js%3A55-56"
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "Missing admin check on `/benefits` (function-level access control)\n\nBoth benefits routes are protected only by `isLoggedIn`; the `isAdmin` middleware exists but is commented out. Any user can GET `/benefits` to list all non-admin users, and POST `/benefits` with an arbitrary `userId` to change any other user's `benefitStartDate`. The DAO returns the complete user documents (including plaintext `password`, `ssn`, `bankAcc`) into the template context."
          },
          "ruleId": "sast/CWE-862/high",
          "ruleIndex": 7
        },
        {
          "level": "error",
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "app/routes/allocations.js%3A16-23"
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "IDOR: allocations looked up by URL `userId`, not session\n\nThe handler reads `userId` from `req.params` rather than `req.session` and never checks it matches the caller. Any logged-in user can request `/allocations/1`, `/allocations/2`, and so on to enumerate every user's name and asset allocation, and user IDs are sequential integers."
          },
          "ruleId": "sast/CWE-639/high",
          "ruleIndex": 8
        },
        {
          "level": "error",
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "app/data/allocations-dao.js%3A77-79"
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "NoSQL injection via `$where` string interpolation\n\nThe `threshold` query parameter from `/allocations/:userId?threshold=` is interpolated unquoted into a MongoDB `$where` JavaScript expression. `threshold=0'; return true; '` returns every allocation document for every user, and `threshold=0'; while(true){}'` pins the database CPU. The `$where` operator executes server-side JavaScript in MongoDB."
          },
          "ruleId": "sast/CWE-943/high",
          "ruleIndex": 9
        },
        {
          "level": "error",
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "app/routes/research.js%3A15-26"
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "SSRF with raw response body reflected as HTML\n\n`/research?symbol=X&url=Y` concatenates two query parameters into a URL and fetches it server-side with `needle.get`. The attacker fully controls the scheme, host, and path, so they can reach cloud metadata endpoints, internal services, or `localhost:27017`. The fetched body is written into the response as `text/html` without encoding, so this is also a reflected XSS and internal-content disclosure channel."
          },
          "ruleId": "sast/CWE-918/high",
          "ruleIndex": 10
        },
        {
          "level": "error",
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "app/routes/contributions.js%3A32-34"
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "Server-side JS injection via `eval()` on POST body\n\nThe contributions update handler passes three fields from `req.body` straight into `eval()`. Any authenticated user (self-registration is open at `/signup`) can POST `preTax=require('child_process').execSync('id').toString()` or `preTax=process.exit()` to `/contributions` and execute arbitrary code in the Node process, or crash the server. The `isNaN` validation runs after the eval, so it does not constrain the payload."
          },
          "ruleId": "sast/CWE-95/high",
          "ruleIndex": 11
        },
        {
          "level": "note",
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "app/views/tutorial/a2.html%3A153%2C%20app/views/tutorial/a3.html%3A176"
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "Tutorial example cookie secret\n\nShort illustrative secret string embedded in an HTML tutorial code sample rather than in executable configuration."
          },
          "ruleId": "secret-scanning/low",
          "ruleIndex": 12
        },
        {
          "level": "warning",
          "locations": [
            {
